  "spec": "github.com/paypal/paypal-rest-api-specifications@90e8041ffe02d80c452d2b476bedd59a8d219bdc openapi/checkout_orders_v2.json and openapi/payments_payment_v2.json",
  "recorded": "api-m.paypal.com (live), 2026-11-12, with a client-credentials token for the public client id; requests that create nothing (empty body, wrong secret)",
  "note": "examples.* are PayPal's published response examples; the server substitutes the order's own id, status and amount. examples.order_not_approved has no example in the spec and follows PayPal's documented error format and issue name (developer.paypal.com/api/rest/reference/orders/v2/errors/#ORDER_NOT_APPROVED). recorded.* are live PayPal bodies, debug_id elided. Live PayPal refused a PayPal-Request-Id of 128 characters and accepted 127 on 2026-11-12; the spec's 108 is the limit this server holds a caller to."
 },
